The embedding i_∞ from the inverse limit D_∞ into the function space [D_∞ → D_∞] is the supremum of the Scott maps iInfTerm n. On an element x it is the supremum over n of i_{n∞} composed with the (n+1)-st component of x and then with j_{∞n}. The supremum is taken in the function space, where suprema of Scott maps are pointwise, so the resulting map is Scott-continuous. `embInfInf.apply` says that evaluating i_∞ at x returns the supremum over n of the values of those summands. The indexed supremum is the supremum of the range of iInfTerm, and evaluating a supremum of Scott maps is pointwise.
